<algorithm id="fig001">
<meta>
<id>273.2</id>
<supertype>AbCd</supertype>
<last_update>2007-09-13</last_update>
</meta>
<title>Suggested evaluation of microscopic hematuria.</title>
<graphic href="eee0641-w0001.gif" />
<cell type="start" id="cell-1">
<label>Microscopic hematuria (at least 3 RBC/HPF on urinalysis).</label>
<path target="cell-2"></path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-2">
<label>Perform a history and physical, evaluating for nonmalignant causes such as urinary tract infection or menstruation. Cause found?</label>
<path target="cell-3">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-5">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-3">
<label>Treat the cause and repeat urinalysis. Persistent hematuria?</label>
<path target="cell-4">No</path>
<path target="cell-5">Yes</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-4">
<label>No further evaluation needed.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-5">
<label>Serum creatinine, cystoscopy, and imaging (CT urogram). Renal and bladder ultrasound is an option instead of CT urogram for younger, lower-risk patients.</label>
<path target="cell-6">Normal</path>
<path target="cell-7">Abnormal</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-6">
<label>Annual urinalysis with microscopy for at least 2 years. If hematuria persists, continue monitoring and consider nephrology referral.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-7">
<label>Treat as appropriate; consider repeat microscopic urinalysis after the condition resolves.</label>
</cell>
<footnotes>
<footnote uid="fn1">RBC/HPF, red blood cells per high-power field.</footnote>
</footnotes>
</algorithm>
<algorithm id="fig002">
<meta>
<id>273.3</id>
<supertype>AbCd</supertype>
<last_update>2007-09-13</last_update>
</meta>
<title>Gross Hematuria: Evaluation.</title>
<graphic href="eee0641-w0002.gif" />
<cell type="start" id="cell-23">
<label>Exclude trauma and hemorrhagic diathesis. Pain present?</label>
<path target="cell-26">No</path>
<path target="cell-25">Yes</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-26">
<label>Clots present?</label>
<path target="cell-29">No clot or unshaped clot</path>
<path target="cell-43">Shaped vermiform (worm-like) clots</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-29">
<label>Cystoscopy.</label>
<path target="cell-32">Positive</path>
<path target="cell-33">Negative</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-32">
<label>Treat cause.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-33">
<label>Upper tract imaging (urography or abdominal CT) and cytology.</label>
<path target="cell-32">Abnormal</path>
<path target="cell-36">Normal</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-36">
<label>Continuation of hematuria?</label>
<path target="cell-42">Microscopic</path>
<path target="cell-41">Gross</path>
<path target="cell-40">Normal</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-40">
<label>No further urologic monitoring.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-41">
<label>Evaluation for primary renal disease.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-42">
<label>UA and cytology at 6, 12, 24, and 36 mo.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-43">
<label>Upper tract imaging.</label>
<path target="cell-46">Abnormal</path>
<path target="cell-47">Normal</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-46">
<label>Treat cause.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-47">
<label>Cystoscopy and cytology.</label>
<path target="cell-46">Abnormal</path>
<path target="cell-36">Normal</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-25">
<label>Type of pain?</label>
<path target="cell-52">Colicky flank pain</path>
<path target="cell-62">Suprapubic pain and/or irritative bladder symptoms</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-52">
<label>Plain abdominal film and renal ultrasound.</label>
<path target="cell-55">Abnormal</path>
<path target="cell-56">Normal</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-55">
<label>Treat cause according to diagnosis.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-56">
<label>Upper tract imaging (urography or abdominal CT).</label>
<path target="cell-55">Abnormal</path>
<path target="cell-59">Normal</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-59">
<label>Continuation of hematuria?</label>
<path target="cell-42">Microscopic</path>
<path target="cell-41">Gross</path>
<path target="cell-69">Normal</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-62">
<label>UA and urine culture.</label>
<path target="cell-65">Abnormal</path>
<path target="cell-70">Normal</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-65">
<label>Treat cause.</label>
<path target="cell-66"></path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-66">
<label>Check with UA after treatment.</label>
<path target="cell-70">Abnormal</path>
<path target="cell-69">Normal</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-69">
<label>No further urologic monitoring.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-70">
<label>Cystoscopy and&#x002F;or cytology.</label>
</cell>
</algorithm>
</algorithms>
